{{Quote|This shotgun blasts a wide burst of high-voltage electricity that arcs between all units—enemy or otherwise—within range.|Armory Description}}

The '''ARC-12 Blitzer''' is an [[Primary Weapon|Primary Energy-Based]] shotgun that fires arcs of electricity instead of buckshot.

== Procurement ==
The Blitzer is unlocked on the 3rd page of the [[Cutting Edge Premium Warbond]] for {{Currency|Medals|80}}.

== Detailed Weapon Statistics ==
{{Attack_Data_Weapon|ARC-12 BLITZER}}

== Attachments ==

{{Attachments Table|Blitzer}}

== Tactical Information ==
* The Blitzer is a unique primary slot weapon due to having truly infinite ammo. If combined with heat based weapons, the wielder will rarely have to worry about their ammo supply.
* Similar to its [[Helldivers 1:AC-5 Arc Shotgun|predecessor]], the Blitzer has very short range, and it may only chain once per arc on a restrictive chain angle. Blitzer however is powerful enough to take down E.G. [[Brood Commander]]s or [[Stalker]]s in a single shock-burst if all the bolts connect with their heads.
** The addition of {{Armor|3|AP}} armor penetration allows Blitzer to sweep off most infantry-class armor alongside reliably stagger enemies like [[Hive Guard|Hive Guards]] at a rate that allows them to be stun-locked.
* Unlike its predecessor (and the [[ARC-3 Arc Thrower]]), the Blitzer has no charge up time prior to shooting, however, it must be pumped after every shot and has a very slow rate of fire.
* The Blitzer possesses high stagger and is good for stun-locking aggressive enemies such as [[Predator Stalker|Predator Stalkers]] or charging [[Alpha Commander|Alpha Commanders]].
* Care should be taken when facing enemies like Heavy Devastators, as the Blitzer's short range and distinct pump/cycle time leaves little room for error; one wrong move (accidentally hitting the Heavy's shield, for instance) will result in a quick death for the wielder unless they are very lucky.
* Like the Arc Thrower, the Blitzer can sometimes prematurely ground itself into obstacles between the desired target and the user, such as corpses or other static objects.
* It is inadvisable to use the Blitzer against the [[Automatons]], due to its incapability to target weak points, and short range. It fares slightly better against the [[Illuminate]], but truly shines against the [[Terminids]], '''especially''' the [[Predator Strain]].
* As can be seen from the damage values of one arc, each salvo with a total damage of 250 is divided into five arcs with damage of 50. Because of this, the total damage per target depends on the number of targets hit by the ARC-12 Blitzer salvo, which affects the time-to-kill.

