== Procurement ==
The Giga Grenade is unlocked on the 2nd page of the [[Entrenched Division Premium Warbond]] for {{Currency|Medals|50}}.

== Detailed Weapon Statistics ==
{{Attack_Data Weapon}}

== Tactical Information ==
* The G-48 Giga Grenade detonates on impact with terrain or an enemy and cannot be cooked. It has the lowest standard capacity of all throwables, at two. However, this is offset by having both the highest damage of all throwables (tied with the [[G-123 Thermite]] and [[G/40-K Melta Mine]]) and the largest blast radius at 12 meters (tied with the [[TED-63 Dynamite]]) in a single device. 
** This combination makes it particularly effective against large enemies, as it can deal significant damage to several body parts at once.
** However, it suffers from an extremely small inner radius of 2 meters.
* The G-48 Giga Grenade benefits from the [[Engineering Kit]], [[Integrated Explosives]], or [[Concussive Padding, Grenadier]] armor passive.
* [[Servo-Assisted]] or [[Desert Stormer]] passives can greatly improve throw range due to the grenade's uniquely low arcing throw.
* [[Supplies#Supply Box|Supply Boxes]] from the [[Resupply]] Stratagem, [[B-1 Supply Pack]] charges, and [[Supplies#Grenade Case|Grenade Case]]s found at [[Minor Places of Interest]] grants full Giga Grenades reserves.
** If the [[Engineering Kit]], [[Integrated Explosives]], or [[Concussive Padding, Grenadier]] armor passive is used, 2 grenades are restored out of the 4 maximum capacity with exception to [[Supplies#Grenade Case|Grenade Case]]s, which restores the full amount.

